              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jo C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Bread in microwave? Asking for a soggy mess! Instead of creme, I used mini marshmallows. I took the advice of other reviewers and put mine in the toaster oven. This with a glass of milk -NOW it's 5 stars.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-10T16:02:13.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rhonda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "in stead of microwaving;put butter on the out side of sandwich and fry it like a grilled cheese sandwich. this is how i had them as a kid.All gooy and delicious. If looking to sweeten it up throw a handfull of chocolote chips in the middle before frying. MMMMMM!!!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-27T12:44:38.013Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "elite99999"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Here's my take: I spread peanut butter on the bread, top with marshmallows (not the creme) and pop in the toaster oven. It gives the bread a nice crunch, makes the peanut butter gooey and gives the marshmallows a nice campfire feel. With my adjustments I give it a five. Great comfort food. Yummo!",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-01T06:29:17.077Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristyann_40"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use a toaster oven to make this yummy treat! I put two pieces of bread in the toaster oven. When the bread is nearly toasted I add 2 marshmallows to one piece of bread. When the marshmallows start to swell, I take it out and add PB to the other slice of bread. I then put the two pieces of bread togather and enjoy the gooey goodness.",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-07T06:44:03.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Holly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This sandwich is even better when cooked in a frying pan like grilled cheese (spray outside of bread with cooking spray). I use torn up marshmallows when camping instead of the fluff spread. AND, this is amazing on cinnamon raisin bread!",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-28T11:46:38.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aresol"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Microwaving this is a bad idea. The bread comes out far too soft and a bit soggy which makes it difficult to hold. Stick with toasting the bread first and then applying the peanut butter and marshmallow and you'll be golden.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-10T21:27:57.877Z"
          },
          {
