              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GoldenWheat8652"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put banana slices on mine as well. I even make Nutella marshmallow fluff and strawberries. Both are so yummy",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-11T17:17:17.575Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TxCin2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'd never had a peanut butter and marshmallow sandwich before. I have heard of Fluffernutters but have yet to see the Fluff sold in stores where I've lived. I did find Marshmallow creme which I understand is similar but not identical. I liked the warm sandwich and the way the marshmallow creme was stringing out and melty. No way was this a pick up and eat sandwich. The warm peanut butter and the warm marshmallow tended to ooze out when taking a bite, making this easier and less messy to eat with a fork. I liked it okay, but didn't think it was worth all the hype. I certainly liked this much better than PB&amp;J. I think this would be good on toast. As it is, that marshmallow creme was pretty darned good right out of the jar just by itself. I might make this again. It was pretty good.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-17T15:20:11.457Z"
          },
